---
/**
 * TEACHING & LEARNING · EXPERIENTIAL & PROJECT-BASED LEARNING — audit §2C.
 *
 * ⚠ THE BANNER IS THE SHARED PageHero AND ITS TREATMENT IS UNTOUCHED — same
 * component, same photograph, same crop, same crumbs, same height, same title
 * and standfirst as before and as every other Academics page. All of the
 * redesign is below it.
 *
 * ⚠ COMBINED PAGE — two of the brief's fourteen bullets: Experiential Learning
 * and Project-Based Learning. The standalone /project-based-learning/ route was
 * an implementation experiment; its verified content is merged here and the
 * route is retired.
 *
 * The page was rebuilt off the generic AcStatement → AcCollage → AcSplit →
 * AcClose system into a composed one: four sections, four different builds — a
 * photo cluster, a drawn path with a real viewer on it, a documentary stack, and
 * a dark close. Everything below the banner lives in
 * components/academics/teaching/ExperientialLearningPage.astro, and that file's
 * frontmatter carries the source for every claim, plus the note on the two
 * activities that are deliberately absent because they cannot be checked.
 *
 * ⚠ SCOPE BOUNDARY — the national science programmes belong to STEM, Robotics &
 * Enrichment; the laboratory inventory to Laboratories & Academic Clubs; the
 * smart-classroom and computer-lab counts to Smart Classrooms & Digital
 * Literacy. This page is about work that produces an object, a venture or a plot.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import ExperientialLearningPage from '../../../components/academics/teaching/ExperientialLearningPage.astro';

import banner from '../../../assets/school-activities/little-agriculturists/02.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
>
  <PageHero
    src={banner}
  />

  {/* ⚠ THE PANEL IS REQUIRED. PageHero is sticky and this panel covers it as the
      page scrolls; without it the banner hangs under the footer.

      ⚠ AND THE PADDING RESET IS AN INLINE STYLE, DELIBERATELY. `.u-page-panel`
      in base.css carries `padding-bottom: var(--sb-section-y)` — 120px of empty
      cream between the closing section and the footer. A stylesheet form of the
      override can be served from a different build than the HTML that needs it,
      and then it silently stops applying; an inline style travels IN the HTML,
      so the two cannot skew. Same decision as the other redesigned pages. */}
  <div class="u-page-panel" style="padding-block: 0;">
    <ExperientialLearningPage />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
